From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] amplifiers: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(amplifiers: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/amplifiers to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - strlcpy() removed, use strscpy() (6.8)
  - ASoC: snd_soc_rtd_to_*() and DAIFMT CBP/CBC naming

Files: cs35l41/cs35l41.c, cs35l45/cs35l45.c, cs35l45/wm_adsp.c, cs40l25/snd-soc-codec-cs40l2x.c, drv2624/drv2624.c, snd_soc_wm_adsp/wm_adsp.c, tas256x/os_layer/src/tas256x-codec.c, tas25xx/src/tas25xx-logic.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline
(7.3). Mechanical renames mirror the upstream tree-wide conversions that removed
the old names:

  * ASoC removed the component wrappers snd_soc_kcontrol_component(),
    snd_soc_component_get_dapm() and snd_soc_component_{force_enable,
    enable,disable,nc}_pin[_unlocked]()/_get_pin_status(). Use
    snd_kcontrol_chip(), snd_soc_component_to_dapm() and the
    snd_soc_dapm_*_pin() calls, which handle the component name prefix
    themselves now (cf. sound/soc/codecs/wm_adsp.c upstream).

Applied to every codec in the project for consistency; lynx builds
cs35l41, cs40l26, snd_soc_wm_adsp and audiometrics.
